{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the degraded service and submitted the mitigation; the endpoint returned `Submission received` for the mitigation stage.\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` deployment's container had only a CPU request and limit. The `memory-limit-quota` ResourceQuota (1Gi memory) rejects any pod that doesn't declare memory, so the `search` ReplicaSet could never create a pod. That left search unavailable for the frontend.\n\n**Fix:** I added a memory request of 128Mi and a limit of 256Mi to the `search` deployment in `hotel-reservation`. The rollout completed, the new pod is Running and registered with Consul, and all pods in the namespace are Running. The quota now shows 128Mi of 1Gi used.\n\nI didn't check end-user latency or traces after the fix, since validation runs on the submission."}}
